# events/tags.conf — how each event gets its display tag.
#
# The dashboard prints one bold tag at the head of every event row, and sorts
# the list by tag before time, so a glance tells you which part of your life an
# event belongs to. This file defines both the tag vocabulary and its order.
#
# Format: one line per rule or declaration, "<Tag>  <something>".
#
# A RULE says how an event earns a tag: "<Tag>  <kind>:<glob>", where <kind> is
# one of three provenances:
#
#     tag:<name>       the event carries <name> in its own tags — the
#                      `tags:` frontmatter of a vault note (case-insensitive).
#     source:<glob>    the event came from this source: an adapter name
#                      (`recurring`) or a feed label from events/feeds.conf
#                      (`the-commons`).
#     title:<glob>     the event's title matches this glob (case-insensitive).
#                      The catch-all for calendars that tag nothing themselves.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom and the FIRST match wins, so order is
# precedence. An event matching no rule is tagged "Other".
#
# A DECLARATION says how a tag is presented: "<Tag>  heading" gives that tag its
# own section on the dashboard — a heading of its own, like Birthdays, with no
# tag on its rows, since the heading already says it. Every tag without such a
# line shares the single "Events" section, where its name leads each row in
# bold. A `heading` line never matches an event; it only declares presentation.
#
# ORDER on screen is the order tags first appear below, declarations included,
# with "Other" last. A heading tag's section sits where its tag first appears,
# and the "Events" section sits where the first non-heading tag appears — so
# moving a block in this file moves it on the dashboard. Within a section,
# events stay in time order (all-day first).
#
# `*` matches any run of characters, `?` a single character; everything else is
# matched literally. '#' comments and blank lines are ignored.

# ── Dance ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A section of its own, and declared first, so the dance socials sit directly
# under Birthdays and above Events.
#
# Provenance: frontmatter. The dance socials live in the notes vault and each
# note is tagged `dance`, so the schedule and the tag travel together.
Dance     heading
Dance     tag:dance

# ── Commons ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provenance: the calendar. Everything on The Commons' Luma feed is Commons,
# whatever it happens to be called.
Commons   source:the-commons

# ── Sailing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provenance: scheduling. The Cal Sailing lesson days are vault notes tagged
# `sailing`, whose times the tides filter rewrites from the club's live hours.
Sailing   tag:sailing
# ...and a safety net for a sailing event arriving from a calendar instead.
Sailing   title:*Cal Sailing*

# Anything unmatched falls through to "Other".
